  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the graph of $y=cot\u2061x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934292/assets/6eb672fe024f024f20c7c3c80947d1b47bade8f998e705d6f411ae3f298ecde2.png)\n\nOur graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. If we rotate the graph ${180}^{\u2218}$ around the origin, we get the same picture. This means that $cot\u2061x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ncot\u2061(-x)=-cot\u2061x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot\u2061(-x) & =-cot\u2061x \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
